  "note": "cs-sandbox b6157c8: two fixes to the agent turn drivers. A turn now runs against one opencode server, where a transient one used to be booted to mint a session id and could be stranded holding the port (SBX-023). And cs-opencode-remote and cs-codex-remote now resolve the learned session id under the turn lock, storing it before releasing: a campaign dispatches the next turn as soon as a reply lands, so turns overlap, and the second one used to mint a session of its own (SBX-024). A new opencode session generates a title, which is a model call no cassette recorded at that point, so the replay missed and the turn died while the campaign waited out its ladder. Validated with make test-smoke on this binary, not make test-integration: all five scenarios PASS on real machines. The race it fixes needs a loaded host to appear, so a local pass does not prove it; cs-campaign's CI is where that is tested. Real-provider traffic was not re-run."
